                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "574aacf1-71c8-3b99-972d-39a58c6ba78d",
                        "entry_id": "917cbc76-89c5-307e-9611-2896ce30b135",
                        "glosses": [
                            "abomasum, maw, rennet-bag, the fourth compartment of the stomach of a ruminant"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "600f5623-3df2-473a-b996-975e8b46fa6d",
                                "sense_id": "574aacf1-71c8-3b99-972d-39a58c6ba78d",
                                "text": "Всё в до́ме стро́го дели́лось: оди́н день обе́д гото́вила ба́бушка из прови́зии, ку́пленной на её де́ньги, на друго́й день прови́зию и хлеб покупа́л дед, и всегда́ в его́ дни обе́ды быва́ли ху́же: ба́бушка брала́ хоро́шее мя́со, а он — требуху́, печёнку, лёгкие, сычу́г.",
                                "translation": "Everything in the household was very strictly shared out: one day Grandmother would get the dinner ready with food she’d bought, and the next day Grandfather bought the food – on those days dinner was invariably worse. Grandmother would buy good quality meat, but Grandfather was content with tripe, liver, lights, or stuffed pig’s belly.",
                                "english": "Everything in the household was very strictly shared out: one day Grandmother would get the dinner ready with food she’d bought, and the next day Grandfather bought the food – on those days dinner was invariably worse. Grandmother would buy good quality meat, but Grandfather was content with tripe, liver, lights, or stuffed pig’s belly."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
